  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Timor-Leste National Social Protection System Strengthened</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Timor-Leste&#x2019;s Government works to build a fair and inclusive social protection system aimed at reducing poverty and inequality, particularly by supporting individuals through key life and work transitions. Despite progress, significant gaps remain in both the legal and effective coverage of social security and health protection. Guided by the National Social Protection Strategy (NSPS) 2021&#x2013;2030, the Government has undertaken reforms to address these challenges.
The ILO supports the implementation of the NSPS. During this biennium, a key contribution is assisting the Ministry of Social Solidarity and Inclusion in developing the Fiscal Space for Social Protection in Timor-Leste policy paper. This paper assesses the financial resources available to the Government by actively identifying and mobilizing potential revenue sources. It serves as a critical tool for operationalizing the strategy and improving its overall efficiency and effectiveness. Importantly, stakeholders now have access to accurate cost estimates and projections, enabling informed decisions on expanding existing programmes or introducing new ones to establish comprehensive social protection floors.
In addition, the ILO provides technical assistance for the development of the Basic Law on Social Protection and other related legal documents, including those outlining the governance framework of the NSPS. Support is also extended to the production of a promotional video on the contributory social security system, as well as to the 2024 update of social protection indicators, which includes revising and analysing the Statistical Bulletin.</narrative>
  </description>
